GEDI L2A Introduction (teaching material)
Arbeitsgruppe Geospatial Technologies, Institut für Geographie und Raumforschung,
Universität Graz

This repository contains material adapted from:

  "Getting Started with GEDI L2A Version 2 Data in Python"
  (python/tutorials/GEDI_L2A_V2_Tutorial.ipynb)
  NASA GEDI-Data-Resources, https://github.com/nasa/GEDI-Data-Resources
  Land Processes Distributed Active Archive Center (LP DAAC).
  Work performed under USGS contract G15PD00467 for NASA contract NNG14HH33I.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see LICENSE).

Modifications: the notebook was restructured and rewritten for a course setting.
Students download regional subsets and clip them to the study area themselves, matplotlib/folium
instead of geoviews/holoviews, reads all beams with a helper function, adds a
DEM-based filter for mountain terrain, exercises, and GeoPackage export.
The waveform (L1B) section was removed. prep/prepare_subset.py is new.

Data:
  Dubayah, R., Hofton, M., Blair, J., Armston, J., Tang, H., Luthcke, S. (2021).
  GEDI L2A Elevation and Height Metrics Data Global Footprint Level V002.
  NASA EOSDIS Land Processes DAAC. https://doi.org/10.5067/GEDI/GEDI02_A.002
  The data files used by the notebook are GEDI L2A files (or subsets of them)
  hosted separately by the instructor.
